TransactionManager:
===================
1.Transaction Manager Automatically initiates the transaction, runs the transaction and comits it.
There are different types of transaction Manager supported by Spring:
1. DataSourceTransactionManager-> JDBC
2. HibernateTransactionManager.
3. JPA Transaction Manager
4. JTA Transaction Manager.

Spring boot chooses the transactionManager on its own, when we give the @transactional annotaion.
if we want to make use of our own transactionmanager i mean if we want to choose it, then we can override it in the 
class annotated with @configuration class.

Example:
=======
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Primary;
import org.springframework.transaction.PlatformTransactionManager;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.EnableTransactionManagement;
import org.springframework.jdbc.datasource.DataSourceTransactionManager;

import javax.sql.DataSource;

@Configuration
@EnableTransactionManagement
public class TransactionConfig {

    @Bean
    @Primary
    public PlatformTransactionManager transactionManager(DataSource dataSource) {
        return new DataSourceTransactionManager(dataSource);
    }
} 
